  "remaining_requirements_note": "The requested wider speed contrast, stronger lead-vehicle slowdown and ten-vehicle traffic comparison are complete. The tables above are the review collection. Whether the following distance is reasonable and prudent remains for review; no legal cutoff has been assumed.",
  "show_internal_ids": false,
  "final_collection": true,
  "viewing_note": "Each table is a separate comparison. Case numbers restart in each table; \u201cCompared against\u201d refers to the other case numbers in that table. \u201cSame reference video\u201d means the identical clip is linked in more than one comparison.\n\nIn the four-panel videos, the upper-left view follows the subject car, the lower-left view follows the lead car, and the two right-hand views look down from cameras that move with the subject car. These are simulator camera views, not route maps. Cars travelling at similar speeds can appear stationary relative to these cameras. The plain road provides few visual cues, so use the measured speed and following-gap overlay to check motion. The arrow-like road silhouette is not a turn instruction; the road is straight with a crest.\n\nThe law\u2019s \u201creasonable and prudent\u201d standard remains a judgment call, so these recordings have no assigned compliant/violation label.",
